caption: General Origin Rules
domain-rule: general-origin-rules

Before the relevant Tradition is mastered, every non-Talent trait granted or purchased through Eldritch Gifts must have both Psionic, -10%, and Super, -10%. Talents do not take either modifier. When an Eldritch Gifts Tradition is mastered, every non-Talent trait purchased through that Tradition becomes eligible to replace both modifiers with Eldritch, -5%, by paying the normal character-point difference. New non-Talent traits purchased through that mastered Tradition may use Eldritch, -5%, from the time of purchase. Traits purchased through an unmastered Eldritch Gifts Tradition retain both Psionic and Super. Domain-wide Eldritch Gifts traits that are not purchased through a specific Tradition become eligible for Eldritch, -5%, once the character has mastered at least one Tier 2 Eldritch Gifts Tradition.

This rule applies even when the Tradition instantiates an Engine from only one structural Origin. Eldritch Gifts Traditions are Domain-specific Psi/Super expressions rather than imports from Riven, Innate Super, or another Domain.
